1
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:08,210
There, that must be it.

2
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:12,420
Wow, it looks like Sora's 
family runs a barbershop.

3
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:15,250
Excuse me!

4
00:00:17,710 --> 00:00:18,920
Oh for Pete's sake...

5
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:22,710
Sorry, but the shop is 
already closed for today.

6
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:24,420
G-good evening.

7
00:00:24,830 --> 00:00:26,330
Who might you be, missy?

8
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:27,460
Um...

9
00:00:28,630 --> 00:00:30,710
I'm... here to make a delivery.

10
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:51,540
Where to go? The land, sea or sky?

11
00:00:50,710 --> 00:00:54,130
Ahiru no Sora

12
00:00:51,630 --> 00:00:54,580
I wanna invite you to come along

13
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:59,420
The pages of our story have started to turn

14
00:01:01,750 --> 00:01:05,170
If you lose your nerve then recycle it

15
00:01:05,170 --> 00:01:08,170
And let it push you past hesitation

16
00:01:08,170 --> 00:01:13,380
Give and go! With the flow

17
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:21,500
Instincts that are buried deep 
will always rear their head again

18
00:01:22,130 --> 00:01:28,710
People can't just hide the 
dreams they once dreamed of

19
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:32,130
Even if these wings can't fly

20
00:01:32,130 --> 00:01:38,960
We want to spread them 
wide and embrace the sky

21
00:01:39,130 --> 00:01:42,290
Becoming the people who we want to be

22
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:49,000
You never know, the impossible 
could be possible tomorrow

23
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,460
So let's keep up the struggle

24
00:01:52,630 --> 00:01:55,500
Happy go ducky!

25
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:07,750
I do apologize for the trouble.

26
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:11,830
The Troublesome Freshman

27
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:11,500
This boy's such a heavy sleeper,
nothing ever wakes him up.

28
00:02:12,210 --> 00:02:16,540
Playing himself to sleep... I swear,
he must have basketballs for brains.

29
00:02:17,330 --> 00:02:19,040
Um, ma'am...

30
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:21,830
You've got his feet poking 
out where his head should be.

31
00:02:22,330 --> 00:02:24,830
Oh, it's fine, it makes no 
big difference either way.

32
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:29,790
Anyway missy, your bangs seem
like they could use a little touch up.

33
00:02:30,130 --> 00:02:30,920
Huh?

34
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:34,500
Since you brought my grandson home,
I'll give you a quick trim.

35
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:36,210
Go sit down.

36
00:02:36,210 --> 00:02:37,500
Um, but I...

37
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:38,790
Enough fussin'.

38
00:02:40,670 --> 00:02:45,250
You're quite the lucky girl,
I only do cuts when I'm in a good mood.

39
00:02:45,420 --> 00:02:48,420
They used to say I was a prodigy
blessed by the gods, ya know.

40
00:02:48,420 --> 00:02:51,460
Your hands are shaking! Are 
you really sure about this?!

41
00:02:56,210 --> 00:02:58,670
You've got some really 
beautiful black hair, missy.

42
00:02:59,250 --> 00:03:00,920
Don't ever go dying it now, ya hear?

43
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:05,080
Something the matter?

44
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:06,170
That picture.

45
00:03:06,790 --> 00:03:07,960
Is she possibly...?

46
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:10,000
Oh, that's just my daughter.

47
00:03:10,830 --> 00:03:12,500
She's also Sora's mother.

48
00:03:13,170 --> 00:03:15,580
Though she's dealing with a 
bit of an illness right now.

49
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:18,540
She's in one of those big, 
fancy government hospitals.

50
00:03:19,210 --> 00:03:21,210
Is it a very serious illness?

51
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:22,000
Huh?

52
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,580
Uh, well, Sora mentioned to me before
that he couldn't see his mother right now.

53
00:03:29,830 --> 00:03:31,630
It's not that he can't.

54
00:03:31,830 --> 00:03:33,460
It's that she won't.

55
00:03:33,830 --> 00:03:34,790
Huh?

56
00:03:35,670 --> 00:03:39,250
That boy used to live deep in the countryside
of the Nagano Prefecture.

57
00:03:39,250 --> 00:03:41,420
It was really out in the middle of nowhere.

58
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,500
A hospital in Kanagawa?

59
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:48,000
Yes. She'll be moving there
for treatment starting next month.

60
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,250
Is her illness going to get 
better if she goes there?

61
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:54,420
Of course. The facilities there 
are much better than ours,

62
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:57,010
and they have many incredibly 
skilled doctors on staff.

63
00:03:57,010 --> 00:04:00,880
Oh really? Then I guess we'll 
be separated for a while.

64
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:02,130
Yes, you will.

65
00:04:02,670 --> 00:04:04,000
Okay then, how about this?

66
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,580
I'll apply for a school in Kanagawa!

67
00:04:06,710 --> 00:04:09,830
If I get into a school that's 
close to where the hospital is,

68
00:04:09,830 --> 00:04:11,360
then I can come see you whenever!

69
00:04:11,630 --> 00:04:14,460
It's best to have someone by your side
in case there's ever trouble!

70
00:04:14,630 --> 00:04:15,580
Right?

71
00:04:16,710 --> 00:04:17,790
No.

72
00:04:17,790 --> 00:04:18,460
Huh?

73
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,330
But why?

74
00:04:21,830 --> 00:04:23,830
I'm not going there for fun.

75
00:04:24,460 --> 00:04:26,790
I'm going to that hospital 
to battle my condition.

76
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:29,080
And I won't be the only one.

77
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:34,080
The doctors and nurses there will also
be helping me to keep fighting against it.

78
00:04:35,250 --> 00:04:39,750
Letting kids like you hang out there all the time,
will only cause trouble for them.

79
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:43,000
That's why I don't need you to come, Sora.

80
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:49,960
Are... you serious?

81
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:53,290
You think I'm a problem just being there?

82
00:04:53,290 --> 00:04:56,830
Do you... not even want 
me to be around, mom?!

83
00:04:57,170 --> 00:04:58,500
Hey, listen Sora.

84
00:04:58,790 --> 00:04:59,580
Your mother just-

85
00:04:59,580 --> 00:05:00,750
Forget it.

86
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:02,000
Sora?

87
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:08,630
Sora! What do you think you're doing?!

88
00:05:09,290 --> 00:05:12,710
Then just go off to Kanagawa
or wherever the hell you want!

89
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:14,460
Even if you beg me...

90
00:05:14,830 --> 00:05:17,000
...I'm never going to come to visit you!

91
00:05:18,290 --> 00:05:19,960
Wait! Sora!

92
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:21,630
I can't believe him.

93
00:05:25,830 --> 00:05:29,330
You know, you're both two peas in a pod.

94
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:34,540
You're both... really bad at lying.

95
00:05:36,130 --> 00:05:40,130
If Sora actually came with 
me all the way to Kanagawa,

96
00:05:40,750 --> 00:05:42,930
I know he would spend every minute he could

97
00:05:42,930 --> 00:05:45,780
at the hospital, both after 
school and on the weekends.

98
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:49,250
And that would mean
he couldn't practice basketball at all...

99
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:51,330
I know.

100
00:05:51,330 --> 00:05:53,670
You don't have to say another word.

101
00:05:54,170 --> 00:05:55,630
I'm so sorry.

102
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:59,750
I just don't want to become 
a burden in Sora's life.

103
00:06:05,460 --> 00:06:08,960
Okay then, take care of 
everything while I'm away.

104
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:10,130
Don't worry about us.

105
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:14,330
We're going to be just fine,
so you stay focused on getting better.

106
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:16,000
Great. Thank you.

107
00:06:16,540 --> 00:06:18,540
Last chance, Sora. Your mom's about to leave.

108
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,710
Bye for now, Sora.

109
00:06:21,710 --> 00:06:24,960
Try to stop being such a picky eater
and learn to clean your plate.

110
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:28,500
And don't forget, you're 
finishing middle school soon.

111
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:31,960
You can't just play basketball all the time,
you have to study hard for your entrance exams.

112
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:33,040
And also-

113
00:06:33,040 --> 00:06:34,630
When I get to high school...!

114
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:38,290
When I get to high school,
I'll join the basketball team right away!

115
00:06:38,710 --> 00:06:41,830
I'll become a way better player than I am now,
and grow way taller!

116
00:06:42,210 --> 00:06:44,170
I'll get on the team's starting lineup!

117
00:06:44,170 --> 00:06:46,880
Then I'll make sure that we 
win our first big tournament!

118
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:47,750
And after all that...!

119
00:06:48,210 --> 00:06:53,380
And after all that... when I'm the very best,
with a perfect record...

120
00:06:54,710 --> 00:07:00,330
Then can I... take our winning trophy...
and come to visit you?

121
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:05,000
Yeah! I'll be waiting!

122
00:07:08,250 --> 00:07:11,000
I've never heard him be so cocky before.

123
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,170
The first tournament that'll 
be held in high school...

124
00:07:13,710 --> 00:07:15,460
...is the national inter-high.

125
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:21,290
We'll never see each other again. Dummy.

126
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:26,210
After that, he took the entrance exams
for schools out here.

127
00:07:26,630 --> 00:07:29,540
And eventually came stumbling into my house.

128
00:07:29,540 --> 00:07:32,130
His dad thought this would 
be the best thing for him.

129
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:35,290
Even though his mom told 
him not to come here?

130
00:07:35,290 --> 00:07:36,250
Yeah.

131
00:07:36,250 --> 00:07:38,540
He's keeping it all a big secret from her.

132
00:07:38,670 --> 00:07:42,080
So that he can go visit her the instant
he wins that tournament.

133
00:07:44,170 --> 00:07:45,210
I see.

134
00:07:45,790 --> 00:07:48,130
Though I already let it slip 
the last time I saw her.

135
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:49,790
That ruins the surprise!

136
00:07:51,170 --> 00:07:53,380
They really do love each other so much.

137
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:56,630
That day, when I told her about it...

138
00:07:57,960 --> 00:08:01,210
...she had the happiest 
look that I've ever seen.

139
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:07,670
He's awake.

140
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:10,170
Wait a second, Sora.

141
00:08:10,630 --> 00:08:11,880
Where are you going?

142
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,420
To school.

143
00:08:14,420 --> 00:08:17,460
I still haven't done my 
1,000 shots for today.

144
00:08:17,960 --> 00:08:20,080
N-no way...

145
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:21,290
Oh, hey.

146
00:08:21,290 --> 00:08:23,460
What are you doing at our place, Madoka?

147
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:24,210
Huh?

148
00:08:24,210 --> 00:08:25,670
He doesn't remember anything?

149
00:08:25,670 --> 00:08:27,290
What a crazy coincidence!

150
00:08:27,290 --> 00:08:29,130
This is actually where I live!

151
00:08:29,420 --> 00:08:34,880
So, uh, does this mean... that match
didn't wear you out enough to skip practice?

152
00:08:35,170 --> 00:08:38,250
I somehow slept a whole 
bunch, so I think I'm okay.

153
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:41,790
That's because you were sleeping
the whole time while I carried you here...

154
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:46,380
But you know, it's already pretty late.
You should just put it off.

155
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:47,830
No, I can't.

156
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:53,670
I can deal with losing a practice match,
but I absolutely cannot lose at the inter-high.

157
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:56,750
I have to practice as much as possible.

158
00:08:57,290 --> 00:08:58,500
Sora...

159
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,330
That's right.

160
00:09:01,330 --> 00:09:03,500
You need to hurry and see your mother again.

161
00:09:07,540 --> 00:09:09,170
Okay, you're all done.

162
00:09:09,170 --> 00:09:10,380
Oh, great.

163
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:10,880
Thanks a lo-

164
00:09:10,880 --> 00:09:12,040
That'll be 1,500 yen.

165
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,000
Huh?

166
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,750
For the cut. 1,500 yen.

167
00:09:14,750 --> 00:09:16,670
Oh wait, did I say this was a favor?

168
00:09:17,130 --> 00:09:19,210
Fine, I'll settle for 1,490 yen.

169
00:09:19,210 --> 00:09:19,830
Pay up.

170
00:09:21,630 --> 00:09:22,710
Okay.

171
00:09:23,210 --> 00:09:24,290
But wait...

172
00:09:28,460 --> 00:09:30,040
...now my bangs are way too short.

173
00:09:35,330 --> 00:09:37,710
I guess I should probably 
get some sleep soon.

174
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:40,750
I ended up staying up 
all night playing games.

175
00:09:41,250 --> 00:09:42,580
But whatever.

176
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:44,210
Today is Sunday, anyway.

177
00:09:50,170 --> 00:09:52,040
Is that one of the elementary kids?

178
00:09:52,040 --> 00:09:56,080
I'm super impressed that they would
get up this early just to practice dribbling.

179
00:09:57,170 --> 00:10:02,540
It's great to see such passion in the youth,
things are looking bright for the future of Japan.

180
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:08,540
Stop the presses. I know that spikey head.

181
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:10,750
Oh jeez, I can't believe him!

182
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:12,750
It's Sunday for Heaven's sake!

183
00:10:13,130 --> 00:10:15,330
Not to mention, it's 5:00 in the morning!

184
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,540
And he just collapsed from 
exhaustion yesterday!

185
00:10:21,170 --> 00:10:22,130
While I'm at it...

186
00:10:35,750 --> 00:10:37,750
He's already made it that far? So quick!

187
00:10:38,420 --> 00:10:41,710
But wait, just how far is he planning to run?

188
00:10:42,710 --> 00:10:44,460
That's the Nikotama line...

189
00:10:44,460 --> 00:10:46,170
Then we've come as far as Setagaya...

190
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:50,830
Oh come on, you can run more than that!

191
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:53,830
I'm so done with this! I swear I'm never
giving piggyback rides ever again!

192
00:10:59,630 --> 00:11:02,790
I had never really noticed this
until Tokiwa pointed it out to me.

193
00:11:03,250 --> 00:11:07,170
But it's obvious that I score significantly fewer shots
when I take them from the left side.

194
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:10,500
Actually, that's not my only problem.

195
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:15,460
His defense was so solid
that I couldn't do anything to get around it.

196
00:11:16,130 --> 00:11:17,290
I have to perfect my drive.

197
00:11:17,750 --> 00:11:19,920
Make it faster! Make it smoother!

198
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:24,380
If I can shake off the defense,
then my odds of scoring will definitely improve!

199
00:11:26,130 --> 00:11:28,330
My two-handed shot still 
needs some work, but...

200
00:11:29,830 --> 00:11:33,500
...if I can work out the kinks, then I can use it
to overcome my weakness on the left side!

201
00:11:35,170 --> 00:11:36,420
I want more skills.

202
00:11:36,750 --> 00:11:38,250
I want to get even better!

203
00:11:38,750 --> 00:11:39,710
HEY!

204
00:11:40,540 --> 00:11:41,630
I'm sorry!

205
00:11:42,670 --> 00:11:44,420
Uh, M-Madoka...?

206
00:11:44,420 --> 00:11:45,710
What are you doing here?

207
00:11:46,170 --> 00:11:52,250
Even the best players in the world, don't go hard
on practice the day after they play a game.

208
00:11:53,170 --> 00:11:57,040
If you keep practicing like this,
you're going to put yourself in the hospital someday.

209
00:11:57,500 --> 00:11:59,460
Madoka's in her casual clothes.

210
00:11:59,460 --> 00:12:00,960
It's kind of exhilarating to see.

211
00:12:01,630 --> 00:12:02,880
Are you listening to me?

212
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,790
I'm listening! I swear!

213
00:12:04,790 --> 00:12:07,460
Well shoot, it looks like somebody
already beat us to the punch.

214
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:10,830
It's Nabe and Chuckie!

215
00:12:11,380 --> 00:12:12,960
And Yasuhara is with them, too!

216
00:12:13,250 --> 00:12:15,210
Can you believe it?

217
00:12:15,210 --> 00:12:17,840
Yasu was so bummed about his ejection 
yesterday that he was like,

218
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:19,900
"let's go do some secret training!"

219
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:22,330
Don't put words in my mouth, dude!

220
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:26,790
I just figured we could kill time
playing some basketball, that's all.

221
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:31,710
Great! Then let's all practice together!

222
00:12:31,710 --> 00:12:34,000
Oh jeez, give me a break already!

223
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:37,540
If you want to practice, then you can just
run yourselves ragged doing it tomorrow!

224
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:41,080
Huh?

225
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:42,670
We're not allowed to practice?

226
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:44,790
Yep. You can't.

227
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:49,040
Use of the court for practice is on a rotation
between the girls' basketball team,

228
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:52,170
the badminton team, and 
also the volleyball team.

229
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:54,290
Hold up, what about us then?!

230
00:12:54,290 --> 00:12:57,540
We had no problem using 
it for practice last week!

231
00:12:57,830 --> 00:13:02,670
That's only because you came here before anyone else
and laid claim to the court, right?

232
00:13:03,290 --> 00:13:07,170
No one had the nerve to say anything.
They were too scared of you.

233
00:13:09,920 --> 00:13:13,420
Then, how about you just 
put us into that rotation?

234
00:13:13,420 --> 00:13:14,920
That's not an option.

235
00:13:15,330 --> 00:13:18,380
If you would like to participate 
as an official school team,

236
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:22,710
then you'll need to find a proper advisor
and also get permission from the principal.

237
00:13:23,290 --> 00:13:26,920
Until you do that, you have no right
to be doing any sort of activities on this court.

238
00:13:27,290 --> 00:13:28,960
Are you picking a fight, old man?!

239
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:29,920
Stop it, Yasu.

240
00:13:30,170 --> 00:13:33,130
Um... so it's okay as long as we
don't use the court, right?

241
00:13:34,290 --> 00:13:35,330
Huh?

242
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:48,170
Well, I get that this isn't 
technically the court but...

243
00:13:48,170 --> 00:13:50,750
Hey Nabe, keep your eyes straight ahead!

244
00:13:50,750 --> 00:13:53,130
Dude, I can't stand to look!

245
00:13:53,130 --> 00:13:58,210
Momoharu said he would talk the principal
into getting us an advisor, so hopefully...

246
00:13:58,210 --> 00:14:00,380
That's assuming it all goes well.

247
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:02,540
BOYS'
BASKETBALL
TEAM

248
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Yo! Welcome back, little bro.

249
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:08,290
The hell are you doing in here, man?

250
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:11,880
Isn't it cool? I found it lying around
behind the supermarket.

251
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:16,830
I paid the principal a visit.

252
00:14:16,830 --> 00:14:18,420
Oh yeah? How'd it go?

253
00:14:19,920 --> 00:14:21,830
He agreed to set us up with an advisor.

254
00:14:22,290 --> 00:14:24,250
But only on one condition.

255
00:14:25,330 --> 00:14:27,450
If we get into any fights, or cause any

256
00:14:27,450 --> 00:14:30,840
other sort of problem, the team 
gets disbanded immediately.

257
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:33,420
I'll give it about a week, then.

258
00:14:33,420 --> 00:14:34,330
We'll see.

259
00:14:35,630 --> 00:14:37,250
Chiaki, be straight with me.

260
00:14:37,790 --> 00:14:40,130
Are you serious about basketball? For real?

261
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:43,170
Hard to say.

262
00:14:43,830 --> 00:14:46,340
After having my passion for 
the game killed back then,

263
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:48,860
I'm not sure it will ever come back.

264
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:51,380
Don't pretend it's not your fault.

265
00:14:51,380 --> 00:14:54,330
You might have been the only 
one running on the court.

266
00:14:54,330 --> 00:14:57,580
But you're still the one who up
and left the game at halftime.

267
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:01,500
That's true.

268
00:15:01,790 --> 00:15:05,130
But I'm nearly there, all I 
need is a little incentive...

269
00:15:05,130 --> 00:15:07,790
...then I think I could reignite my passion.

270
00:15:07,790 --> 00:15:09,000
I'm so close.

271
00:15:09,460 --> 00:15:10,790
Just one thing!

272
00:15:10,790 --> 00:15:11,920
Chiaki...

273
00:15:13,170 --> 00:15:14,630
S'cuse me!

274
00:15:15,130 --> 00:15:18,750
We are, like, totally hoping to be managers
for the basketball team!

275
00:15:19,290 --> 00:15:21,710
Passion reignited. Let's do this.

276
00:15:24,540 --> 00:15:27,790
We were stuck on the stage
for the entire practice session.

277
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,090
There's not much we can do.

278
00:15:30,090 --> 00:15:33,860
We're still too new at this
to be practicing how to shoot, anyway.

279
00:15:33,860 --> 00:15:37,790
We're not going to make much progress
by practicing basketball without a basket, though.

280
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:48,380
Holy shit!

281
00:15:48,710 --> 00:15:50,920
Even a newbie like me can tell...

282
00:15:51,420 --> 00:15:53,330
...this guy is probably an expert!

283
00:15:56,750 --> 00:15:58,920
H-he's giving me goosebumps!

284
00:16:00,330 --> 00:16:00,960
Yo!

285
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:01,830
Huh?

286
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:04,880
You've got really sick basketball skills.

287
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:09,210
Is this ball yours? It's really worn out.

288
00:16:09,580 --> 00:16:10,880
How'd you do that move?

289
00:16:11,460 --> 00:16:12,790
Could you show us again?

290
00:16:14,460 --> 00:16:16,460
We're members of the basketball team.

291
00:16:16,460 --> 00:16:19,710
But to be honest, we hardly even know
how to dribble the ball.

292
00:16:19,830 --> 00:16:22,380
From what I just saw, you dribble like a pro.

293
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,630
It was almost as if the ball
was glued to your hand or something.

294
00:16:26,460 --> 00:16:29,960
So, do us a favor and show 
us those sick moves again.

295
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:35,040
The gym isn't the only place with a basket!

296
00:16:35,210 --> 00:16:37,830
I can practice shooting if I do it over here!

297
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,170
Yasuhara!

298
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:47,000
What the hell do you think 
you're doing, punk?!

299
00:16:47,330 --> 00:16:48,710
I'm no "punk."

300
00:16:49,330 --> 00:16:50,540
The name's Kite.

301
00:16:51,460 --> 00:16:55,170
Do I need to teach you a lesson
in proper manners? Well, senpai?

302
00:16:57,830 --> 00:17:00,380
I think this punk has a few screws loose.

303
00:17:00,830 --> 00:17:02,040
All right, then.

304
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:04,960
Let's see what you can teach 
after I pound your face in!

305
00:17:07,630 --> 00:17:08,540
Chuckie!

306
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,580
You're too slow. This 
won't even be a challenge.

307
00:17:11,790 --> 00:17:13,960
Cocky bastard! I'll knock you down a peg!

308
00:17:19,170 --> 00:17:21,040
Who even... is this guy?

309
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:23,420
What're you lookin' at, shrimp?

310
00:17:23,580 --> 00:17:25,000
You want a lesson, too?

311
00:17:25,670 --> 00:17:27,630
I doubt you could even put up a fight.

312
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:29,630
It'd be like me crushing an ant.

313
00:17:30,290 --> 00:17:31,710
Don't take me so lightly.

314
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:34,330
You crossed the line.

315
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:34,330
CALCIUM BAR

316
00:17:34,580 --> 00:17:36,130
And I'm gonna make you pay for it!

317
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:40,210
As a 100th degree black belt in karate,
I'll pound you into the dirt!

318
00:17:41,170 --> 00:17:43,170
Quit your bullshit!

319
00:17:45,380 --> 00:17:47,380
Why attack me, Yasuhara?

320
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:48,710
You just stay out of this!

321
00:17:49,210 --> 00:17:51,460
That surprise attack was a cheap move, man.

322
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:56,580
Just so you know, I'm a legit
2nd degree black belt in karate.

323
00:17:56,920 --> 00:18:01,830
But I'm a little clumsy, so I'm not good
at pulling my punches. Sorry in advance.

324
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:04,710
Okay. Bring it on.

325
00:18:06,710 --> 00:18:08,040
That's enough!

326
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:10,210
Momoharu!

327
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:13,000
Don't lay a hand on him, Yasu.

328
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:14,830
Why the hell not?!

329
00:18:14,830 --> 00:18:16,500
I'll explain things later.

330
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:17,670
Just bear with it.

331
00:18:19,330 --> 00:18:21,830
This doesn't bode well for 
the future at all, dammit.

332
00:18:22,210 --> 00:18:25,830
Sorry man, we can't afford
to be getting into any fights right now.

333
00:18:26,080 --> 00:18:28,460
So let's all just call 
it quits for today. Deal?

334
00:18:29,250 --> 00:18:30,630
Wait a damn minute.

335
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,540
You can't just expect to 
turn tail and run from me.

336
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:35,960
I don't give a shit about your problems.

337
00:18:36,830 --> 00:18:38,500
What are you trying to get at?

338
00:18:38,830 --> 00:18:40,540
I can tell from the look in your eyes.

339
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:42,330
You're the boss of this group.

340
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:44,540
Greased
Lightning

341
00:18:44,580 --> 00:18:45,750
So fight me.

342
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:47,670
He's got tattoos!

343
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:52,080
Whatever the case,
I've already decided to retire from fighting.

344
00:18:52,420 --> 00:18:54,960
I've got more important things to do
than waste time dealing with idiots like-

345
00:19:01,130 --> 00:19:02,250
So fast!

346
00:19:02,750 --> 00:19:04,420
You're just as slow as them.

347
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:08,830
Momoharu!

348
00:19:14,040 --> 00:19:17,330
Did he seriously just counter 
that kick with a headbutt?!

349
00:19:17,710 --> 00:19:20,210
Don't make me have to repeat myself, dammit.

350
00:19:20,630 --> 00:19:22,540
I can't fight you right now.

351
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,460
Are you a member of the 
basketball team like them?

352
00:19:27,670 --> 00:19:28,460
Yep.

353
00:19:29,080 --> 00:19:30,380
That's just wonderful.

354
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,210
Now I've got something to look forward to.

355
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:37,580
Wh-what exactly happened between you guys?

356
00:19:37,580 --> 00:19:41,380
Hell if I know. He just came swinging at me
out of nowhere.

357
00:19:42,750 --> 00:19:44,460
Is something wrong, Momoharu?

358
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:46,750
Take a good look.

359
00:19:47,130 --> 00:19:49,380
Do you see the last spot 
that he was standing in?

360
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:53,500
He was almost all the way back to where
the three-point line would be.

361
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:55,170
And what about it?

362
00:19:55,580 --> 00:19:56,960
You didn't notice?

363
00:19:57,210 --> 00:19:59,170
In the blink of an eye 
that jerk managed to...

364
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:03,790
...fly all the way to where I 
was with just a single bound.

365
00:20:05,630 --> 00:20:08,750
He must never skip leg day
with explosive power like that...

366
00:20:14,420 --> 00:20:17,380
BOYS'
BASKETBALL
TEAM

367
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:17,330
So we get disbanded if we 
cause any trouble at all?

368
00:20:17,710 --> 00:20:19,920
I see, that explains your attitude yesterday.

369
00:20:19,920 --> 00:20:22,330
Yep. Fights are out of the question.

370
00:20:22,670 --> 00:20:25,410
I asked around my class for some 
info and found out that guy

371
00:20:25,410 --> 00:20:27,740
had been suspended up until yesterday.

372
00:20:28,440 --> 00:20:29,830
He's totally bad news.

373
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:34,420
But, you know, he was still 
really good at basketball.

374
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:50,080
I know it's time for practice,
but aren't we stuck on the stage again?

375
00:20:50,380 --> 00:20:52,630
Playing without a basket really sucks.

376
00:20:53,420 --> 00:20:55,210
I must be going crazy or something.

377
00:20:55,210 --> 00:20:57,830
I actually want to see how well
that punk from yesterday can play.

378
00:21:01,710 --> 00:21:02,750
What's this?

379
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:05,170
What's the matter?

380
00:21:05,170 --> 00:21:06,330
Did something happen?

381
00:21:11,330 --> 00:21:12,880
Outta my way, losers!

382
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:14,420
That dumbass!

383
00:21:14,420 --> 00:21:15,830
Shit! Somebody stop him!

384
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:18,830
Stop! Stop!

385
00:21:19,250 --> 00:21:21,460
We aren't allowed to use the court right n-

386
00:21:27,330 --> 00:21:28,170
Huh?

387
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:36,380
Look out!

388
00:21:44,670 --> 00:21:45,920
Now he's done it!

389
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:47,790
Are you all right, Yoshino?!

390
00:21:47,790 --> 00:21:49,960
Wait! We shouldn't move her around!

391
00:21:50,630 --> 00:21:52,830
Hang in there, Yoshino!

392
00:21:52,830 --> 00:21:54,040
Yoshino?

393
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:57,330
Shit. This is a disaster.

394
00:22:14,790 --> 00:22:18,130
It didn't matter how long 
you stared up at the sky

395
00:22:18,130 --> 00:22:21,420
You always said that you 
would never be able to fly

396
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:24,630
One night I cried wondering 
how long it would take

397
00:22:24,790 --> 00:22:28,000
Until I could finally reach you with my hands

398
00:22:28,130 --> 00:22:31,500
Eventually I got used to just running away

399
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:34,790
Until the day I realized that was a weakness

400
00:22:34,790 --> 00:22:39,000
So let's start it all over, right now

401
00:22:41,630 --> 00:22:47,630
The things precious to us 
were always close at hand

402
00:22:47,630 --> 00:22:53,960
We are never completely alone 
at any time in our lives

403
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:57,290
The truth is that you can 
fly, wherever you want

404
00:22:57,290 --> 00:23:01,040
Spreading your wings to go 
far higher than anyone else

405
00:23:01,250 --> 00:23:05,290
The more tears that you shed

406
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:07,250
Then the stronger you become

407
00:23:07,250 --> 00:23:10,630
Let's use those wings 
to travel the world over

408
00:23:10,630 --> 00:23:14,210
And find a path to a future 
that no one knows about

409
00:23:14,210 --> 00:23:18,790
Always, always, always

410
00:23:18,960 --> 00:23:22,460
Walking onwards, all of us together

411
00:23:30,500 --> 00:23:35,460
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: The Duck
and the Kite

412
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:33,830
Next time: "The Duck and the Kite."

